<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 9 June, from 68 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nero" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">68 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,958 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Nero takes his own life</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Declared a public enemy by the Senate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> died at a freedman's villa outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His death ended the Julio-Claudian dynasty and opened the Year of the Four Emperors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">747 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,279 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abu Muslim launches an open revolt against Umayyad rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-muslim">Abu Muslim</a>, a Persian revolutionary and military commander, began an open revolt against Umayyad rule. The Abbasid revolution brought down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> in 750, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> that replaced it ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1311">1311 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">715 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Duccio's Maestà is installed in Siena Cathedral</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duccio">Duccio di Buoninsegna</a>'s Maestà, a huge double-sided altarpiece of the Virgin and Child commissioned by the city of Siena in 1308, was carried in procession around the city and installed in Siena Cathedral.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duccio">Duccio di Buoninsegna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1772">1772 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">254 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rhode Island colonists burn the British schooner Gaspee</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The British revenue schooner HMS Gaspee, which enforced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/navigation-acts">Navigation Acts</a>, ran aground off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwick-rhode-island">Warwick, Rhode Island</a>, and that night men led by Abraham Whipple and John Brown boarded and burned her. The affair heightened tensions before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspee-affair">Gaspee affair</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress of Vienna signs its Final Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>, the great powers signed the treaty redrawing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s map after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. Its settlement shaped European borders and diplomacy for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Dickens dies at Gad's Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dickens died at his Kent home aged 58, leaving The Mystery of Edwin Drood unfinished. His novels of poverty and injustice had made him the most popular author of his age.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Donald Duck makes his screen debut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Donald Duck first appeared in the Disney short The Wise Little Hen. His temper and garbled voice made him one of the studio's most popular characters.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Secretariat wins the Belmont by 31 lengths</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretariat set a world record for the distance and became the first US Triple Crown winner in 25 years. His Belmont time still stands as the race record.</p></div></li></ol>
